NNAAMMEE
     aaccccttoonn — enable/disable system accounting

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     aaccccttoonn [_f_i_l_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     With an argument naming an existing _f_i_l_e, aaccccttoonn causes system accounting
     information for every process executed to be placed at the end of the
     file.  If no argument is given, accounting is turned off.

     To have aaccccttoonn enabled at boot time, use “rcctl enable accounting”, which
     sets

           accounting=YES

     in rc.conf.local(8).

     Log rotation of the default accounting file, _/_v_a_r_/_a_c_c_o_u_n_t_/_a_c_c_t, is per‐
     formed by the daily(8) maintenance script.

FFIILLEESS
     /var/account/acct  default accounting file

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The aaccccttoonn utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     lastcomm(1), acct(2), acct(5), daily(8), sa(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The aaccccttoonn command first appeared in Version 7 AT&T UNIX.

